                <pb facs="0626" n="510" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg510"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/5034: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-06-09T20:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 9, 1923—8
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 9—1:12 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>211. My 210, June 9, 2 p.m. Strike ended. Reasons obscure. No change in Peking.
                    Koo has just informed me that he has requested President to drop his name from
                    further consideration for premiership.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
